The attached image (Figure 2 from the 2017 npj Vaccines paper) illustrates that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles remain largely localized at the injection site and are cleared over time in mice. Panel **a** shows the fluorescent signal confined to the calf muscles post-injection, decreasing in intensity over 21 days. Panel **b** demonstrates that by Day 21, fluorescence is predominantly at the injection sites with minimal presence in internal organs, confirming limited systemic distribution. Panel **c** quantifies the fluorescence intensity at the injection site, showing an initial rapid decrease, a slight increase by Day 2, and a gradual decline, with about 20% of the original signal detected by Day 21, supporting Nano-11's transient presence and clearance.